H5200.definition:
patronymic from H5199 (נְטֹפָה);
a Netophathite, or inhabitant of Netophah
KJV: Netophathite.

H5201.definition:
a primitive root;
to guard; figuratively, to cherish (anger)
KJV: bear grudge, keep(-er), reserve.

H5202.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5201 (נָטַר);
to retain
KJV: keep.

H5203.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pound, i.e. smite; by implication (as if beating out, and thus expanding) to disperse; also, to thrust off, down, out or upon (inclusively, reject, let alone, permit, remit, etc.)
KJV: cast off, drawn, let fall, forsake, join (battle), leave (off), lie still, loose, spread (self) abroad, stretch out, suffer.

H5204.definition:
a doubtful word; apparently from H5091 (נָהָה);
lamentation
KJV: wailing.

H5205.definition:
from H5110 (נוּד);
motion (of the lips in speech)
KJV: moving.

H5206.definition:
feminine of H5205 (נִיד);
removal, i.e. exile
KJV: removed.

H5207.definition:
or נִיחֹחַ; from H5117 (נוּחַ);
properly, restful, i.e. pleasant; abstractly, delight
KJV: sweet (odour).

H5208.definition:
(Aramaic) or נִיחֹחַ; (shorter) (Aramaic), corresponding to H5207 (נִיחוֹחַ);
pleasure
KJV: sweet odour (savour).

H5210.definition:
of foreign origin;
Nineveh, the capital of Assyria
KJV: Nineveh.

H5211.definition:
from H5127 (נוּס);
fugitive
KJV: that fleeth.

H5212.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Nisan, the first month of the Jewish sacred year
KJV: Nisan.

H5213.definition:
from H5340 (נָצַץ);
a spark
KJV: spark.

H5214.definition:
a root probably identical with that of H5216 (נִיר), through the idea of the gleam of a fresh furrow;
to till the soil
KJV: break up.

H5215.definition:
or נִר; from H5214 (נִיר);
properly, plowing, i.e. (concretely) freshly plowed land
KJV: fallow ground, plowing, tillage.

H5216.definition:
or נִר; also נֵיר; or נֵר; or (feminine) נֵרָה; from a primitive root (see H5214 (נִיר); H5135 (נוּר)) properly, meaning to glisten;
a lamp (i.e. the burner) or light (literally or figuratively)
KJV: candle, lamp, light.

H5217.definition:
a primitive root;
to smite, i.e. drive away
KJV: be viler.

H5218.definition:
or נָכָא; from H5217 (נָכָא);
smitten, i.e. (figuratively) afflicted
KJV: broken, stricken, wounded.

H5219.definition:
from H5218 (נָכֵא);
properly, a smiting, i.e. (concretely) an aromatic gum (perhaps styrax) (as powdered)
KJV: spicery(-ces).

H5220.definition:
from an unused root meaning to propagate;
offspring
KJV: nephew, son's son.

H5221.definition:
a primitive root;
to strike (lightly or severely, literally or figuratively)
KJV: beat, cast forth, clap, give (wounds), [idiom] go forward, [idiom] indeed, kill, make (slaughter), murderer, punish, slaughter, slay(-er, -ing), smite(-r, -ing), strike, be stricken, (give) stripes, [idiom] surely, wound.

H5222.definition:
from H5221 (נָכָה);
a smiter, i.e. (figuratively) traducer
KJV: abject.

H5224.definition:
probably of Egyptian origin;
Neko, an Egyptian king
KJV: Necho. Compare H6549 (פַּרְעֹה נְכֹה).

H5225.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן); prepared;
Nakon, probably an Israelite
KJV: Nachon.

H5226.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be straightforward;
properly, the fore part; used adverbially, opposite
KJV: before, over against.

H5227.definition:
from the same as H5226 (נֵכַח);
properly, the front part; used adverbially (especially with preposition), opposite, in front of, forward, in behalf of
KJV: (over) against, before, direct(-ly), for, right (on).

H5228.definition:
from the same as H5226 (נֵכַח);
straightforward, i.e. (figuratively), equitable, correct, or (abstractly), integrity
KJV: plain, right, uprightness.

H5229.definition:
feminine of H5228 (נָכֹחַ);
properly, straightforwardness, i.e. (figuratively) integrity, or (concretely) a truth
KJV: equity, right (thing), uprightness.

H5230.definition:
a primitive root;
to defraud, i.e. act treacherously
KJV: beguile, conspire, deceiver, deal subtilly.

H5233.definition:
from an unused root meaning to accumulate;
treasure
KJV: riches, wealth.

H5234.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to scrutinize, i.e. look intently at; hence (with recognition implied), to acknowledge, be acquainted with, care for, respect, revere, or (with suspicion implied), to disregard, ignore, be strange toward, reject, resign, dissimulate (as if ignorant or disowning)
KJV: acknowledge, [idiom] could, deliver, discern, dissemble, estrange, feign self to be another, know, take knowledge (notice), perceive, regard, (have) respect, behave (make) self strange(-ly).

H5235.definition:
or נֹכֶר; from H5234 (נָכַר);
something strange, i.e. unexpected calamity
KJV: strange.

H5236.definition:
' from H5234 (נָכַר);
foreign, or (concretely) a foreigner, or (abstractly) heathendom
KJV: alien, strange ([phrase] -er).

H5237.definition:
from H5235 (נֶכֶר) (second form);
strange, in a variety of degrees and applications (foreign, non-relative, adulterous, different, wonderful)
KJV: alien, foreigner, outlandish, strange(-r, woman).

H5238.definition:
probably for H5219 (נְכֹאת);
spicery, i.e. (generally) valuables
KJV: precious things.

H5239.definition:
apparently a primitive root;
to complete
KJV: make an end.

H5241.definition:
apparently for H3223 (יְמוּאֵל);
Nemuel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Nemuel.

H5242.definition:
from H5241 (נְמוּאֵל);
a Nemuelite, or descendant of Nemuel
KJV: Nemuelite.

H5243.definition:
a primitive root;
to become clipped or (specifically) circumcised
KJV: (branch to) be cut down (off), circumcise.

H5244.definition:
feminine from H5243 (נָמַל);
an ant (probably from its almost bisected form)
KJV: ant.

H5245.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5246 (נָמֵר)
{a leopard (from its stripes)}
KJV: leopard.

H5246.definition:
from an unused root meaning properly, to filtrate, i.e. be limpid (comp H5247 (נִמְרָה) and H5249 (נִמְרִים)); and thus to spot or stain as if by dripping;
a leopard (from its stripes)
KJV: leopard.

H5247.definition:
from the same as H5246 (נָמֵר); clear water;
Nimrah, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Nimrah. See also H1039 (בֵּית נִמְרָה), H5249 (נִמְרִים).

H5248.definition:
or נִמְרֹד; probably of foreign origin;
Nimrod, a son of Cush
KJV: Nimrod.

H5249.definition:
plural of a masculine corresponding to H5247 (נִמְרָה); clear waters;
Nimrim, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Nimrim. Compare H1039 (בֵּית נִמְרָה).

H5250.definition:
probably from H4871 (מָשָׁה); extricated;
Nimshi, the (grand-) father of Jehu
KJV: Nimshi.

H5251.definition:
from H5264 (נָסַס);
a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token
KJV: banner, pole, sail, (en-) sign, standard.

H5252.definition:
feminine participle passive of H5437 (סָבַב);
properly, an environment, i.e. circumstance or turn of affairs
KJV: cause.

H5253.definition:
a primitive root;
to retreat
KJV: departing away, remove, take (hold), turn away.

H5254.definition:
a primitive root;
to test; by implication, to attempt
KJV: adventure, assay, prove, tempt, try.

H5255.definition:
a primitive root;
to tear away
KJV: destroy, pluck, root.

H5256.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5255 (נָסַח)
{to tear away}
KJV: pull down.

H5257.definition:
from H5258 (נָסַךְ);
properly, something poured out, i.e. a libation; also a molten image; by implication, a prince (as anointed)
KJV: drink offering, duke, prince(-ipal).

H5258.definition:
a primitive root;
to pour out, especially a libation, or to cast (metal); by analogy, to anoint aking
KJV: cover, melt, offer, (cause to) pour (out), set (up).

H5259.definition:
a primitive root (probably identical with H5258 (נָסַךְ) through the idea of fusion);
to interweave, i.e. (figuratively) to overspread
KJV: that is spread.

H5260.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5258 (נָסַךְ);
to pour out a libation
KJV: offer.

H5261.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5262 (נֶסֶךְ);
a libation
KJV: drink offering.

H5262.definition:
or נֵסֶךְ; from H5258 (נָסַךְ);
a libation; also a cast idol
KJV: cover, drink offering, molten image.

H5263.definition:
a primitive root;
to wane, i.e. be sick
KJV: faint.

H5264.definition:
a primitive root; to gleam from afar, i.e. to be conspicuous as a signal; or rather perhaps a denominative from H5251 (נֵס) (and identical with H5263 (נָסַס), through the idea of a flag as fluttering in the wind);
to raise a beacon
KJV: lift up as an ensign.

H5265.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pull up, especially the tent-pins, i.e. start on ajourney
KJV: cause to blow, bring, get, (make to) go (away, forth, forward, onward, out), (take) journey, march, remove, set aside (forward), [idiom] still, be on his (go their) way.

H5266.definition:
a primitive root;
to go up
KJV: ascend.

H5267.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5266 (נָסַק)
{to go up}
KJV: take up.

H5268.definition:
of foreign origin;
Nisrok, a Babylonian idol
KJV: Nisroch.

H5269.definition:
from H5128 (נוּעַ); motion;
Neah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Neah.

H5270.definition:
from H5128 (נוּעַ); movement;
Noah, an Israelitess
KJV: Noah.

H5271.definition:
or נָעֻר; and (feminine) נְעֻרָה; properly, passive participle from H5288 (נַעַר) as denominative;
(only in plural collectively or emphatic form) youth, the state (juvenility) or the persons (young people)
KJV: childhood, youth.

H5272.definition:
from H5128 (נוּעַ) and H410 (אֵל); moved of God;
Neiel, a place in Palestine
KJV: Neiel.

H5273.definition:
from H5276 (נָעֵם);
delightful (objective or subjective, literal or figurative)
KJV: pleasant(-ure), sweet.

H5275.definition:
or (feminine) נַעֲלָה; from H5274 (נָעַל);
properly, a sandal tongue; by extension a sandal or slipper (sometimes as a symbol of occupancy, a refusal to marry, or of something valueless)
KJV: dryshod, (pair of) shoe((-latchet), -s).

H5276.definition:
a primitive root;
to be agreeable (literally or figuratively)
KJV: pass in beauty, be delight, be pleasant, be sweet.

H5277.definition:
from H5276 (נָעֵם); pleasure;
Naam, an Israelite
KJV: Naam.

H5278.definition:
from H5276 (נָעֵם);
agreeableness, i.e. delight, suitableness, splendor or grace
KJV: beauty, pleasant(-ness).

H5279.definition:
feminine of H5277 (נַעַם); pleasantness;
Naamah, the name of an antediluvian woman, of an Ammonitess, and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Naamah.

H5280.definition:
patronymic from H5283 (נַעֲמָן);
a Naamanite, or descendant of Naaman (collectively)
KJV: Naamites.

H5281.definition:
from H5278 (נֹעַם); pleasant;
Noomi, an Israelitess
KJV: Naomi.

H5282.definition:
from H5276 (נָעֵם);
pleasantness (plural as concrete)
KJV: pleasant.

H5283.definition:
the same as H5282 (נַעֲמָן);
Naaman, the name of an Israelite and of a Damascene
KJV: Naaman.

H5284.definition:
patrial from a place corresponding in name (but not identical) with H5279 (נַעֲמָה);
a Naamathite, or inhabitant of Naamah
KJV: Naamathite.

H5285.definition:
from an unused root meaning to prick;
probably a brier; by implication, a thicket of thorny bushes
KJV: thorn.

H5286.definition:
a primitive root;
to growl
KJV: yell.

H5287.definition:
a primitive root (probably identical with H5286 (נָעַר), through the idea of the rustling of mane, which usually accompanies the lion's roar);
to tumble about
KJV: shake (off, out, self), overthrow, toss up and down.

H5288.definition:
from H5287 (נָעַר);
(concretely) a boy (as active), from the age of infancy to adolescence; by implication, a servant; also (by interch. of sex), a girl (of similar latitude in age)
KJV: babe, boy, child, damsel (from the margin), lad, servant, young (man).

H5289.definition:
from H5287 (נָעַר) in its derivative sense of tossing about;
a wanderer
KJV: young one.

H5290.definition:
from H5287 (נָעַר); (compare H5288 (נַעַר))
(abstractly) boyhood
KJV: child, youth.

H5291.definition:
feminine of H5288 (נַעַר);
a girl (from infancy to adolescence)
KJV: damsel, maid(-en), young (woman).

H5292.definition:
the same as H5291 (נַעֲרָה);
Naarah, the name of an Israelitess, and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Naarah, Naarath.

H5293.definition:
from H5288 (נַעַר); youthful;
Naarai, an Israelite
KJV: Naarai.

H5294.definition:
from H5288 (נַעַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); servant of Jah;
Nearjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Neariah.

H5295.definition:
from H5288 (נַעַר); juvenile;
Naaran, a place in Palestine
KJV: Naaran.

H5296.definition:
from H5287 (נָעַר);
something shaken out, i.e. tow (as the refuse of flax)
KJV: tow.

H5297.definition:
a variation of H4644 (מֹף);
Noph, the capital of Upper Egypt
KJV: Noph.

H5298.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to spring forth; a sprout;
Nepheg, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Nepheg.

H5299.definition:
from H5130 (נוּף) in the sense of lifting;
a height; also a sieve
KJV: border, coast, region, sieve.
